        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;lab/relid.py: just relid&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Indexes every Address Library id CommonLibSSE-NG names: RELOCATION_ID, REL::RelocationID, REL::ID and REL::VariantID sites in include/ and src/ (a function when a func_t decltype precedes the site), Offsets_VTABLE.h's arrays, Offsets_RTTI.h and Offsets_NiRTTI.h. Derived data: regenerated, never edited." tooltip="Source: lab/relid.py:2-18; justfile:98-100 (relid)" id="re1-b4">
          <mxCell style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#0E8088;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=3;spacingBottom=3;strokeWidth=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="re1-col2">
            <mxGeometry x="10" y="33" width="310" height="100" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;lab/relids.tsv&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;se, ae, vr, kind, name, slot, file, line: 17,941 rows, as 258043 206143 vtable VTABLE_ValueModifierEffect Offsets_VTABLE.h:1953. It names 13631 (UIMessageQueue::AddMessage), 16024 (InventoryEntryData::PoisonObject) and 104651 (NativeFunctionBase::Call), but not poison's 40481, 40482, 41044, 41069 or 38386, from the re-analyst's Ghidra read, nor 55631, 55500 and 51648, hud-trace.js's caller frames." tooltip="Source: lab/relids.tsv (17,942 lines with its header; looked up 2026-10-13); docs/verbs/poison.md:41-61; docs/verbs/shouts.md:450-458" id="re1-b5">
          <mxCell style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=3;spacingBottom=3;strokeWidth=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;shape=note;size=12;boundedLbl=1;" vertex="1" parent="re1-col2">
            <mxGeometry x="10" y="163" width="310" height="124" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;addrlib/&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Address Library database for SkyrimSE 1.6.1170, versionlib-1-6-1170-0.bin (format 2). Gitignored, downloaded from Nexus by Eli, read-only to the agent." tooltip="Source: CLAUDE.md:52-53 (Workspace layout); lab/addr.py:2-21" id="re1-b1">
          <mxCell style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=3;spacingBottom=3;strokeWidth=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;shape=cylinder3;boundedLbl=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=10;spacingTop=12;" vertex="1" parent="re1-col2">
            <mxGeometry x="10" y="317" width="310" height="74" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;lab/addr.py: just addr &amp;lt;id&amp;gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Reads the database exactly as CommonLibSSE-NG's REL::IDDatabase does (REL/Relocation.h: header_t::read, unpack_file), tested against CommonLib's versionlib-1-6-353-0.bin fixture. Strict: a missing id is an error, where CommonLib's lower_bound returns the next id's offset (--commonlib-quirk reproduces that)." tooltip="Source: lab/addr.py:2-22; lab/tests/test_addr.py; justfile:94-96 (addr)" id="re1-b2">
