        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;a. Dual casting&lt;/b&gt;" tooltip="Source: docs/verbs/spell-cast.md (Playtest fourteen)" id="re3-la">
          <mxCell style="swimlane;horizontal=0;startSize=34;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#FFFFFF;swimlaneFillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#999999;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;container=1;collapsible=0;recursiveResize=0;" vertex="1" parent="re3-1">
            <mxGeometry x="20" y="250" width="1780" height="300" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="Eli, 2026-10-12: &quot;we'll also have to account for dual casting as well&quot;. The client reports isDualCasting and the server never read it. How many streams does the game run for two hands of one spell, and how many does the server count?" tooltip="Source: docs/verbs/spell-cast.md:455-466" id="re3-la-cap">
          <mxCell style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=3;spacingBottom=3;strokeWidth=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="re3-la">
            <mxGeometry x="44" y="8" width="1720" height="30" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;1 Probe x-dual-cast, run 20261013-054049&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;On parity c918a7a1, c1 held Flames in both hands (Home and End, 4 s each, 234 ms apart) at c2 150 units ahead: two casts, not a dual cast, with no perk and no common press. c1's game charged both (24.2 magicka a second with both hands) and raised a hit series per hand every 200 ms, each event twice. The client sent one series: hitService.ts drops a caster's magic hit within 100 ms of its last. The server counted one stream, 19 hits and 3.63 stream-seconds (casts.rs claim() gives a hit to the first open stream of its spell). c2 lost 8.1 Health a second, ending at 0.734, inside b-spell's one-stream band." tooltip="Source: docs/verbs/spell-cast.md:467-498; session scratchpad x-dual-cast.yaml; lab/results/20261013-054049-x-dual-cast.json" id="re3-a1">
          <mxCell style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#0E8088;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=3;spacingBottom=3;strokeWidth=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="re3-la">
            <mxGeometry x="44" y="44" width="261.6667" height="212" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;2 The static lead&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;CommonLibSSE-NG annotates ValueModifierEffect's GetAllowMultipleCastingSourceStacking (vfunc 0x11, V/ValueModifierEffect.h:18) as { return 1; }, where ActiveEffect's (A/ActiveEffect.h:79) is { return 0; }: a value modifier from each hand would stack. Flames' damage, MGEF 0x13CA9, is a Value Modifier on Health (lab/esm.py). UESP: without the perk, the same effectiveness as though cast normally, but twice; a forum answer had said a fire spell's effect overwrites itself." tooltip="Source: docs/verbs/spell-cast.md:499-519; CommonLibSSE-NG include/RE/V/ValueModifierEffect.h:18, include/RE/A/ActiveEffect.h:79; lab/frida/effect-stack-trace.js:1-11" id="re3-a2">
          <mxCell style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#4D4D4D;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=3;spacingBottom=3;strokeWidth=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="re3-la">
            <mxGeometry x="335.6667" y="44" width="261.6667" height="212" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="re3-a2-b0" value="&lt;b&gt;HYPOTHESIS&lt;/b&gt;" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#595959;strokeColor=#595959;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontSize=9;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=3;spacingBottom=3;strokeWidth=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;rounded=1;arcSize=50;spacingTop=0;spacingBottom=0;spacingLeft=0;spacingRight=0;" vertex="1" parent="re3-a2">
          <mxGeometry x="8" y="192" width="73" height="15" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;3 Frida: effect-stack-trace.js in probe x-dual-stack, run 20261013-061434&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;In c1's game, on ValueModifierEffect's Update (vfunc 0x04) and ModifyActorValue (0x20) through its vtable, Address Library 206143. The right hand alone: one Flames effect on c2's figure (castingSource 1, magnitude -8), about 26 calls of each per 500 ms. Both hands: two effect objects at once, hands 1 and 0, each modifying about 25 times per 500 ms through 4.5 s. Its offset check failed at Actor+0x98 (page 1)." tooltip="Source: docs/verbs/spell-cast.md:509-536; lab/frida/effect-stack-trace.js; session scratchpad x-dual-stack.yaml, stack-read.py; lab/results/20261013-061434-x-dual-stack.json (frida/c1-effect-stack-trace.js.jsonl)" id="re3-a3">
          <mxCell style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#0E8088;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=3;spacingBottom=3;strokeWidth=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="re3-la">
            <mxGeometry x="627.3333" y="44" width="261.6667" height="212" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="re3-a3-b0" value="&lt;b&gt;CONFIRMED&lt;/b&gt;" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#1A1A1A;strokeColor=#1A1A1A;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontSize=9;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=3;spacingBottom=3;strokeWidth=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;rounded=1;arcSize=50;spacingTop=0;spacingBottom=0;spacingLeft=0;spacingRight=0;" vertex="1" parent="re3-a3">
          <mxGeometry x="8" y="192" width="69" height="15" as="geometry" />
