        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;a. A lead held; a reading did not&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;CommonLib's { return 1; } annotation held: two hands, two working effects, measured. In the same script a header comment read as (SE and AE, VR) put the MagicTarget at +0x98, and its own runtime check caught it; the script now measures the offset instead of reading it (page 1)." tooltip="Source: docs/verbs/spell-cast.md:509-536; lab/frida/effect-stack-trace.js:15-17, :118-133; git log 101c71b" id="re3-sa">
          <mxCell style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F2F2F2;strokeColor=#999999;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=3;spacingBottom=3;strokeWidth=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="re3-lessons">
            <mxGeometry x="10" y="33" width="576" height="64" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;b. The trace saw what a screenshot missed&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;x-reteach-probe's screenshot after teachword and a 5 s wait shows no notice, while hud-trace.js caught the word-of-power message and its caller. The check on the fix asserts the word unlocked; its notice check rests on screenshots." tooltip="Source: docs/verbs/shouts.md:450-458; session scratchpad x-reteach-probe.yaml, reteach/s-009-c1.png, x-reteach2.yaml; lab/results/20261013-072218-x-reteach2.json" id="re3-sb">
          <mxCell style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F2F2F2;strokeColor=#999999;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=3;spacingBottom=3;strokeWidth=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="re3-lessons">
            <mxGeometry x="602" y="33" width="576" height="64" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;c. A trace can act, not only watch&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;poison-trace.js answered the box by calling its callback, then kept it shut by rewriting its show message, where tapped keys and close-menu could not; b-poison keeps the same frida step, so the scenario depends on the script." tooltip="Source: lab/frida/poison-trace.js:11-27, :84-112; docs/verbs/poison.md:220-259; lab/scenarios/b-poison.yaml:38" id="re3-sc">
          <mxCell style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F2F2F2;strokeColor=#999999;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=3;spacingBottom=3;strokeWidth=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="re3-lessons">
            <mxGeometry x="1194" y="33" width="576" height="64" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
